<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">States Brabant</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Staats-Brabant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">States Brabant (Staats-Brabant) was the northern part of the Duchy of Brabant conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in the Eighty Years' War, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/s-hertogenbosch">'s-Hertogenbosch</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breda">Breda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergen-op-zoom">Bergen op Zoom</a>. Confirmed to the Republic by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-munster">Peace of Münster</a> in 1648, it was governed directly by the States General as a Generality Land without a vote of its own, and its Catholic majority faced restrictions. It became the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant">North Brabant</a> after 1796.</p></div>
